---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Our promise — CanYouDo?">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap-narrow">
      <p class="kicker">Our promise</p>
      <h1>Look after the worker, and the work looks after itself.</h1>
      <p style="font-size:1.1rem;color:var(--ink-600)">Most gig platforms compete by squeezing the person doing the work. CanYouDo? was built on the opposite bet.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:44px">The problem with race-to-the-bottom cleaning</h2>
      <p>When a platform takes a big cut of a low hourly rate, the cleaner ends up rushing between too many jobs for too little money. Corners get cut, good people quit, and customers churn through a revolving door of strangers. Nobody wins — the platform just loses slowest.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:40px">Our bet: supported workers, delighted customers</h2>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li><strong>£15/hour, kept in full.</strong> Cleaners are paid directly by customers. We never take commission from their rate — our £5/hour introduction fee is charged separately and transparently.</li>
        <li><strong>Bonuses for measurable quality.</strong> Punctuality, completed checklists and genuine ratings earn up to £50/month extra. Good work literally pays.</li>
        <li><strong>Tools that respect their time.</strong> Availability they control, a portal with all their bookings, direct messaging with clients, and automatic email notifications so nothing gets missed.</li>
        <li><strong>Independence, not gig-serfdom.</strong> Cleaners set their own schedule, keep their own clients, and hold their own insurance. We introduce; they run their business.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top:40px">What that means for customers</h2>
      <p>A cleaner who is fairly paid, rewarded for quality and treated like a professional turns up on time, cares about your instructions and stays with you for the long term. Continuity and care — the two things you actually want from a cleaner — come from how the person is treated. That's the whole model.</p>

      <h2 style="margin-top:40px">Straight answers about what we are</h2>
      <p>CanYouDo? is an <strong>online introduction service</strong> — think of it as a well-run notice board with a booking system attached. We are not a cleaning company or an employer. Cleaners are independent providers responsible for their own public liability insurance and tax; customers and cleaners contract with each other directly. We're upfront about this because trust is the product.</p>

      <p style="margin-top:36px">Questions? Email <a href="mailto:hello@canyoudo.uk">hello@canyoudo.uk</a> — customer service is handled personally, not by a ticket robot.</p>

      <p style="margin-top:26px">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/find-a-cleaner/">Find a cleaner</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/signup/?role=cleaner" style="margin-left:10px">Join as a cleaner</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
